    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Dynamic Sun</title>
    <style>
        .sun {
            width: 50px;
            height: 50px;
            background: yellow;
            border-radius: 50%;
            transition: background 0.5s ease;
        }

        .sun.day {
            background: yellow;
        }

        .sun.sunset {
            background: red;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <?php if ($current_time >= 6 && $current_time <= 19) : ?>
        <div class="sun sun.day"></div>
    <?php elseif ($current_time > 19 || $current_time < 6) : ?>
        <div class="sun sun.sunset"></div>
    <?php endif; ?>
</body>
</html>
```

In this example, we first get the current time using the `date()` function in PHP. Then, we use a conditional statement to determine whether it's day or sunset. Based on the condition, we apply different CSS classes to the `<div>` element with the class "sun". The `transition` property is used to smoothly transition between the two styles.

